        "original_id": "b02d2c1e-cc63-59b0-896e-90841eed7f4f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: Dixit Dominus, HWV 232\n- People: George Frideric Handel\n- Places: Halle, Hamburg, Italy, London\n- Topics: Baroque music, psalm settings, nationality\n\nFacts:\n- George Frideric Handel was born as Georg Friedrich Händel on 23 February 1685 (O.S.) / 5 March 1685 (N.S.).\n- George Frideric Handel received important training in Halle and later worked as a composer in Hamburg and Italy.\n- George Frideric Handel settled in London in 1712 and spent the bulk of his career there.\n- George Frideric Handel became a naturalised British subject in 1727.\n- George Frideric Handel was a German, later British, baroque composer known for his operas, oratorios, anthems, and organ concertos.\n- George Frideric Handel died on 14 April 1759.\n- Dixit Dominus is a psalm setting by George Frideric Handel catalogued as HWV 232.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
